      "content": "The yellowing leaves on your Monstera deliciosa could be due to a few possible reasons. Overwatering is a common issue, as it can lead to root rot, causing the lower leaves to turn yellow and droop. Make sure to check the soil moisture before watering, and consider repotting the plant in a well-draining potting mix if symptoms persist. Additionally, under-fertilization or nutrient deficiencies might also contribute to the issue, so consider using a balanced fertilizer during the growing season.",
